# StringLike is a union bound, so its parameter admits reference types only. A
# `str` conforms to Text as a value, but a StringLike parameter takes its
# `stringView`: `print g.stringView`, `h == g.stringView`. Before the rule the
# comparison passed the checker and reached the C with mismatched operands.
main: function is {
    g: "hello".str to: 32
    print g
    h: "hello".string
    if h == g then print "eq"
}
